WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Raj: Each zone forms a separate failure domain.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.568
Lukas: For power, yes. What about shared configuration pushes?

3
00:00:08.568 --> 00:00:13.103
Anika: Managed configuration currently updates both zones together.

4
00:00:13.103 --> 00:00:16.607
Hannah: So a bad rule could remove both paths.

5
00:00:16.607 --> 00:00:20.879
Priya: Just to confirm, staged updates required, right?

6
00:00:20.879 --> 00:00:25.775
Raj: Yes, separate approval gates and tested last-good versions.

7
00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:30.527
Lukas: Let me play that back. Geography isn't independence.

8
00:00:30.527 --> 00:00:34.558
Anika: That's our blast radius even without hardware failure.

9
00:00:34.558 --> 00:00:39.070
Hannah: The single point of failure is operational, perhaps.

10
00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:43.990
Priya: Okay, record correlated failures alongside physical ones.

